11
00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:25.710
even though you wore it as a badge of honor.

12
00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:29.010
I was wondering, I always opt for optimism

13
00:00:29.010 --> 00:00:32.380
no matter how hard it is to get there, I will get there,

14
00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:35.190
what was it like to grow up with a moniker

15
00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:36.997
like "Sunshine Girl"?

16
00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:39.950
Yeah. So, I think it's both

17
00:00:39.950 --> 00:00:42.580 line:15%
such a blessing and a curse at the same time,

18
00:00:42.580 --> 00:00:43.453 line:15%
because,

19
00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:49.600 line:15%
I felt very important with that moniker

20
00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.660
because I thought I made people happy, you know?

21
00:00:52.660 --> 00:00:56.202
And that was a good thing to be labeled "Sunshine Girl".

22
00:00:56.202 --> 00:00:58.740
Where it didn't serve me well

23
00:00:58.740 --> 00:01:01.860
was that I then never felt like I could complain

24
00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.177
or say, "this doesn't feel good,

25
00:01:04.177 --> 00:01:05.630
"I don't like this so."

26
00:01:05.630 --> 00:01:08.940
And then as I grew up and in my relationships

27
00:01:08.940 --> 00:01:10.520
and,

28
00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:12.470
I sort of became mute

29
00:01:12.470 --> 00:01:15.650
because I would rather not ruffle anyone's feathers,

30
00:01:15.650 --> 00:01:16.760
not stir the mud.

31
00:01:16.760 --> 00:01:18.640
And you know, it took me a long time

32
00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.507
