Yeah, there was definitely (chuckles) a lack of stability,

51
00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:15.443
and that's for sure.

52
00:02:15.443 --> 00:02:18.170
I mean, I have to say the amount of people

53
00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:20.750
that have responded in terms of being able to relate

54
00:02:20.750 --> 00:02:22.520
to what I was going through as a child,

55
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:26.030
it might not have been as chaotic and crazy,

56
00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:29.870
but it is pretty an amazingly universal thing

57
00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.560
when you are from divorced parents

58
00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:36.330
who really, I shouldn't...

59
00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:39.487
I mean, my mother who I have a great relationship with now

60
00:02:39.487 --> 00:02:41.180
and I always really have,

61
00:02:41.180 --> 00:02:43.160
I was always sort of a momma's girl and all,

62
00:02:43.160 --> 00:02:45.500
I was always trying to defend her,

63
00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:48.390
but my mother put herself before her children.

64
00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:50.410
And she'll tell me that now she admits it,

65
00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:51.550
it's why I could write the book,

66
00:02:51.550 --> 00:02:53.010
I had her blessing to write the book

67
00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:57.200
because she really owns what she did when she was younger.

68
00:02:57.200 --> 00:02:59.960
And that's pretty remarkable too.

69
00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:02.770
We were at her whim and that's hard as a child,

70
00:03:02.770 --> 00:03:04.400
and you have no control over that.

71
00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.120 line:15%
What I did have control over

72
00:03:06.120 --> 00:03:08.000 line:15%
was the temperature in the room,

73
00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:09.690 line:15%
emotional temperature in the room.

74
00:03:09.690 --> 00:03:13.150 line:15%
I felt like I could actually change it,

75
00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:16.040
you know, by being sunny and happy and,

76
00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.010
I don't think we realize

77
00:03:18.010 --> 00:03:20.210
